NEARS-3527 — AC4: live-reproduce PRE-FIX unguarded behavior (baseline PoC)

Approach used: live in-place code swap on the SAME running Store-Panel instance
(booted from this ticket's own worktree, DB isolated to a disposable clone
multi_food_db_test_qa3527). Standing up a second full app instance for the base
branch was judged unnecessary overhead given the diff is a single file; instead:

  1. Confirmed exact diff between feat/userapp-reskin2 (pre-fix) and this
     worktree's HEAD (post-fix) for the one changed file:
       git show feat/userapp-reskin2:Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Vendor/CustomRoleController.php
       diff <that> Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Vendor/CustomRoleController.php
     Diff is exactly: + ALLOWED_MODULES const, + Rule::in(...) on modules.* in
     both store() and update(), + 'modules.*.in' message — nothing else.
  2. Backed up the post-fix file, overwrote the live worktree file with the
     git-show'd PRE-FIX content, cleared config/route/view cache.
  3. Logged in as vendor ts@ts.com (store 35) via /login/vendor.
  4. POSTed to /vendor-panel/custom-role/create with:
       name[]=QA-PREFIX-BASELINE-POC
       modules[]=order
       modules[]=admin_only_key      <- NOT one of the 27 real checkbox values,
                                          never rendered anywhere in create.blade.php
  5. Result: HTTP 302 (success — no validation error), and the row WAS persisted:

     SELECT id,name,modules,store_id FROM multi_food_db_test_qa3527.employee_roles
       WHERE name='QA-PREFIX-BASELINE-POC';
     -> id=11 name=QA-PREFIX-BASELINE-POC modules=["order","admin_only_key"] store_id=35

     This is the live-reproduced vulnerability: a modules[] value that is not one
     of the 27 legitimate checkboxed keys is accepted and written verbatim to
     EmployeeRole.modules on the CURRENT (pre-fix) code, exactly matching the
     ticket's own evidence block (raw assignment, no whitelist).

  6. Immediately restored the post-fix file (cp back from backup), verified
     `git status --short` on the controller file was clean (byte-identical to
     the committed post-fix version), cleared caches again.
  7. Re-ran the IDENTICAL POST (fresh CSRF token, name=QA-POSTFIX-REVERIFY) against
     the restored post-fix code: HTTP 302 back to the create form, toastr
     'Invalid module selected', and NO row was created for that name — see
     ac5-negative-store.log for the full negative-case evidence.

Net: the pre-fix vulnerability was reproduced LIVE (not just code-read) as its
own artifact (row id=11, still present in the disposable clone for inspection),
and the fix's rejection of the identical payload was independently re-confirmed
immediately after restoring the real code. The disposable DB clone
(multi_food_db_test_qa3527) was dropped at the end of this QA run; row id=11's
content is preserved verbatim in this log file.
